SUMMARY:How to Marry a Millionaire | Matinee Classics
DESCRIPTION:Three New York models—Shatze (Lauren Bacall)\, Pola (Marily
 n Monroe)\, and Loco (Betty Grable)—set up in an exclusive apartment wi
 th a plan: tired of cheap men and a lack of money\, they intend to use al
 l their talents to snag three millionaires. The trouble is what happens w
 hen real love comes along? Co-starring William Powell in his second-to-la
 st movie role\, Cameron Mitchell\, Rory Calhoun\, Fred Clark\, and David 
 Wayne\, How to Marry a Millionaire was the first comedy to be shot in Cin
 emaScope and the second film to ever use the format. [95 min\; comedy\; E
 nglish]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Three New York models—Shatze (Lauren 
 Bacall)\, Pola (Marilyn Monroe)\, and Loco (Betty Grable)—set up in an 
 exclusive apartment with a plan: tired of cheap men and a lack of money\,
  they intend to use all their talents to snag three millionaires. The tro
 uble is what happens when real love comes along? Co-starring William Powe
 ll in his second-to-last movie role\, Cameron Mitchell\, Rory Calhoun\, F
 red Clark\, and David Wayne\, <i>How to Marry a Millionaire</i> was the f
 irst comedy to be shot in CinemaScope and the second film to ever use the
  format. [95 min\; comedy\; English]</p>
